#[summary("메서드 구문 증명: 수신자 조정, 고유 impl, 경계 trait, 계약의 메서드 (ADR-0051, 2M-01)")]
mod mt {
    struct Counter { n: u64, cap: u64 }

    struct Stack<T: Copy> { items: [T; 4], len: usize }

    impl Counter {
        spec fn room(self: &Counter) -> bool {
            self.n < self.cap
        }

        spec fn within(self: &Counter) -> bool {
            self.n <= self.cap
        }

        spec fn ticked(self: &Counter, before: Counter) -> bool {
            self.n == before.n + 1 && self.cap == before.cap
        }

        spec fn fresh(self: &Counter, cap: u64) -> bool {
            self.n == 0 && self.cap == cap
        }

        #[effects(pure)]
        #[uses(Counter::fresh)]
        fn new(cap: u64) -> (r: Counter)
            ensures r.fresh(cap),
        {
            Counter { n: 0, cap: cap }
        }

        #[effects(pure)]
        #[uses(Counter::room, Counter::ticked)]
        fn tick(self: &mut Counter) -> ()
            requires self.room(),
            ensures self.ticked(*old(self)),
        {
            self.n = self.n + 1;
        }

        #[effects(pure)]
        #[uses(Counter::within, left_of)]
        fn left(self: &Counter) -> (r: u64)
            requires self.within(),
            ensures left_of(self, r),
        {
            self.cap - self.n
        }
    }

    spec fn left_of(c: &Counter, r: u64) -> bool {
        r == c.cap - c.n
    }

    spec fn has_room<T: Copy>(s: &Stack<T>) -> bool {
        s.len < 4
    }

    spec fn grew<T: Copy>(before: Stack<T>, after: Stack<T>) -> bool {
        after.len == before.len + 1
    }

    spec fn two(r: usize) -> bool {
        r == 2
    }

    spec fn percent(r: i64) -> bool {
        0 <= r && r <= 100
    }

    spec fn twice_percent(r: i64) -> bool {
        0 <= r && r <= 200
    }

    impl<T: Copy> Stack<T> {
        #[effects(pure)]
        fn size(self: &Stack<T>) -> usize {
            self.len
        }

        #[effects(pure)]
        #[uses(has_room, grew)]
        fn push(self: &mut Stack<T>, x: T) -> ()
            requires has_room::<T>(self),
            ensures grew::<T>(*old(self), *self),
        {
            self.items[self.len] = x;
            self.len = self.len + 1;
        }
    }

    trait Score {
        #[effects(pure)]
        fn score(self: &Self) -> (r: i64)
            ensures percent(r);

        #[effects(pure)]
        #[uses(percent, twice_percent)]
        fn doubled(self: &Self) -> (r: i64)
            ensures twice_percent(r),
        {
            self.score() + self.score()
        }
    }

    impl Score for Counter {
        #[effects(pure)]
        #[uses(percent)]
        fn score(self: &Counter) -> (r: i64)
            ensures percent(r),
        {
            if self.n < 100 { i64::try_from(self.n).unwrap() } else { 100 }
        }

        #[effects(pure)]
        #[uses(percent, twice_percent)]
        fn doubled(self: &Counter) -> (r: i64)
            ensures twice_percent(r),
        {
            self.score() * 2
        }
    }

    #[effects(pure)]
    #[uses(percent)]
    fn best<T: Copy + Score>(a: &T, b: &T) -> (r: i64)
        ensures percent(r),
    {
        let x: i64 = a.score();
        let y: i64 = b.score();
        if x < y { y } else { x }
    }

    spec fn enough(cap: u64) -> bool {
        2 <= cap
    }

    spec fn two_less(cap: u64, r: u64) -> bool {
        r == cap - 2
    }

    #[effects(pure)]
    #[uses(enough, two_less, Counter::fresh, Counter::room, Counter::ticked, Counter::within, left_of)]
    fn run(cap: u64) -> (r: u64)
        requires enough(cap),
        ensures two_less(cap, r),
    {
        let mut c: Counter = Counter::new(cap);
        c.tick();
        c.tick();
        c.left()
    }

    #[effects(pure)]
    #[uses(has_room, grew)]
    fn fill(x: i64) -> usize {
        let mut s: Stack<i64> = Stack { items: [0; 4], len: 0 };
        s.push(x);
        s.push(x);
        s.size()
    }

    #[effects(pure)]
    #[uses(twice_percent)]
    fn both(c: &Counter) -> (r: i64)
        ensures twice_percent(r),
    {
        c.doubled()
    }
}
